{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/434702-question-about-2nd-ed-forsaken","id":434702,"title":"Question about 2nd Ed Forsaken","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-09T15:27:22-07:00","id":434702,"title":"Question about 2nd Ed Forsaken","content":"First I love Forsaken as a game. The below is far less of a criticism as something that confuses me about the world itself.<br /> <br /> But their was an issue I saw with first edition and I'm curious if it is still present in second edition.<br /> <br /> In first edition the core idea was the werwolves were basically spirit cops. Their duty was to keep spirits on one side, and humans on the other.<br /> This makes sense but it breaks down a bit if you think of it too much. How?<br /> <br /> Well the book continues to argue the lack of forsaken. So this means that their must be areas of the world where their are no Forsaken present. This means technically<br /> the spirit world is left unchecked? If this is true then has the world in those areas collapsed? If not then really what purpose do the Forsaken have is it just busy work? Similarly what about areas where the Forsaken are not really equipped to be present, say deep in the ocean? While there may be pure present they have far different views of how the spirit world is supposed to be.<br /> <br /> So first. Am I missing something in the above logic? Or is this just one of those, just accept it it's the conceit to make the game work view.<br /> <br /> Second did 2nd ed do anything to approach this break in the game world?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5285-huntsfromshadow","name":"huntsfromshadow","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T15:39:27-07:00","id":434732,"title":"","content":"Spirits don't really tend to... blatantly shred the gauntlet and wreak havoc everywhere. My view is that what happens in areas that lack Forsaken (as well as any other supernaturals that might fulfill that duty in their absence, like certain mages or hunters) is that you get more &quot;haunted&quot; areas, you have more people acting weird because they're urged or claimed, there's more stories of cursed objects and areas, things like that. Very few spirits would just collapse civilization around them.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T15:52:02-07:00","id":434746,"title":"","content":"Second edition doesn't remove this idea of the Forsaken as inheriting the duty of monitoring the divide between flesh and spirit, but it does shift the emphasis some. There's much more emphasis on the instincts of the Uratha and their inborn nature as predators and hunters; the unifying theme of the book is &quot;the wolf must hunt,&quot; and there's an understanding that werewolves don't really do these things <i>primarily</i> out of a feeling of spiritual obligation. That feeling is still communicated, but ultimately, the Uratha assemble into packs and bring low men and spirits because that's what they do; it's natural to them in a way that isn't shared with mortal humans.<br /> <br /> Aside from that, yeah; there <i>are</i> many places where the Forsaken have no presence or influence, but the result isn't spirits pushing through the Gauntlet willy-nilly, as falco says. There's some conveyance of the feeling that spirits spend a lot of time half dormant, so while an area may be thickly populated in the Shadow, not all of those spirits are conversing or scheming or running around at any given time. When they do push through the Gauntlet, which is difficult without outside influence, they can cause bizarre supernatural predation and chaos, yes, but there is a vision of the World of Darkness as a place where that simply happens in a lot of areas. People keep their heads down. If a spirit insists on doing something that people can't keep their heads down about, well, the Hunter: the Vigil book is right next door, but usually, people find a way to keep themselves mentally in a world where those things can be pushed out of mind.<br /> <br /> The effect of having a Forsaken pack watching over your neighborhood isn't (usually; but game campaigns tend to focus on exceptionally interesting places and times!) to save it from becoming an unrecognizable, otherworldly bloodbath. It's to sweep the corners and curb excesses. It prevents having that dark spot in the alley or the back of the forest where people disappear every so often, or come back changed, not remembering what happened to them. It makes sure the flow of Essence doesn't dry up and enervate the will of the people living there. It makes things calmer and more reasonable.<br /> <br /> Assuming that's what the pack wants to accomplish and they're good at accomplishing it. Neither of those are givens, either. Maybe they just want to rule the roost. That's very human, after all, and they're half human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T17:41:29-07:00","id":434894,"title":"","content":"If a tree falls in a forest and no one is around to hear it, does it make a sound? Sorry, but I had to. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Without people around to muck around with the world, I think spirits would reflect a world that takes care of itself. I guess their human side keeps them from doing the logical thing, kill all humans. I think the new edition is supposed to move away from &quot;spirit cop.&quot; It sounds more like &quot;spirit predator.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T18:30:40-07:00","id":434997,"title":"","content":"The 2ed sums up all werewolf is about by this phrase: <b>&quot;The Wolf Must Hunt&quot;</b>. Hunting is quintessential for a Uratha in the same way that blood is for vampires. They don't just hunt spirits, basically anything can be a target of the hunt, to spirits, the Hosts, the Claimed, humans(both as individuals and institutions), other werewolfs, other supernaturals, etc, everything and everyone that don't match with their vision of territory and is a threat to the pack(both the werewolfs and the friends, family they adopt into the pack). 2ed really drives hope the brutal nature of the Hunt for the werewolfs, more than 1ed it is really a <b>game of savage fury.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T19:26:01-07:00","id":435124,"title":"","content":"Humans generate more Essence. It's their nature. The way their emotions explode so vividly is what creates large amounts of Essence and the way their emotions fluctuate wildly thickens the Gauntlet. In the wilderness and in the deep ocean, there's less Essence being generated, so most of the spirits go dormant despite the weaker Gauntlet. With fewer spirits around, what Essence exists isn't as hotly contested, so there's much less impetus to flee from predation or manipulate material-side creatures.<br /> <br /> Uratha defend humans. Hishu is based on humans for this reason: the Herd is human. Most other creatures have spirits of their own and it's much less likely that they'll be preyed upon by spirits, but humans are particularly vulnerable to spiritual predation because of the breadth of emotion they are capable of generating: most spirits can find a way to make a human generate Essence resonant with their desired munchies, whereas a spirit of loyalty is going to be completely stymied if they try to Urge an angler fish.<br /> <br /> Now having read this, look up the Four Noble Truths of Buddhism and read them as a how-to guide on not being Claimed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T19:51:56-07:00","id":435156,"title":"","content":"Kind of an interesting question. First edition was ostensibly more about dark mystery than dark brutality. It wasn't like oWoD, where it's our world, but worse, with sin run rampant. It was more our world, but more mysterious. There were conspiracies and things in the shadows, and stranger things behind those things, and even they had strings being pulled by mysterious forces.<br /> <br /> Second edition seems to have kept the mystery but gone and embraced the more evil aspects. The Strix are bad enough when they prey on vampires, but what they do to humanity is often worse. The cults of the God Machine often involve weird sacrifice, maybe even that of life. Of course, it's all happenin through the lens of dark mystery. Or else we wouldn't have so many glorious 'What is this thing?' threads.<br /> <br /> Whether other parts of the world have gone to hell or not is going to depend entirely on your game, but it certainly seems like if there's not werewolves around, the claimed, shartha, ridden or Pure or Bale Hounds or idigam are. Did you read the fiction? Thousands died. It's pretty brutal even when the werewolves are on the hunt. While the writers probably wouldn't do it, it's easy to imagine a lot of the bad aspects of our world magnified by the spirits and other Things of the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> As for the ocean, I don't think nature on its own is a perfect balance. Stuff happens, even without humanity. But there's a lot less stuff probably happening down there, or if it is happening, werewolves wouldn't really be able to see the results until the stars are right or nuclear testing awakens some ancient beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-09-2015, 10:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T02:37:06-07:00","id":435498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/434702-question-about-2nd-ed-forsaken?p=434746#post434746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second edition doesn't remove this idea of the Forsaken as inheriting the duty of monitoring the divide between flesh and spirit, but it does shift the emphasis some. There's much more emphasis on the instincts of the Uratha and their inborn nature as predators and hunters; the unifying theme of the book is &quot;the wolf must hunt,&quot; and there's an understanding that werewolves don't really do these things <i>primarily</i> out of a feeling of spiritual obligation. That feeling is still communicated, but ultimately, the Uratha assemble into packs and bring low men and spirits because that's what they do; it's natural to them in a way that isn't shared with mortal humans.<br /> <br /> Assuming that's what the pack wants to accomplish and they're good at accomplishing it. Neither of those are givens, either. Maybe they just want to rule the roost. That's very human, after all, and they're half human.</div> </div> </div> </div>You must also remember that 2ed is highlighting the humans <b>as a Prey </b>- it's whole shtick of nowdays Iron Masters. Humanity can be <i>bad</i> in setting, on itself. Serial killers are <b>not</b> guided by murder spirits - they are <b>creating</b> murder spirits. Bored and powerful human elite can summon Maeljins and their servants. Humanities hunters are <i>real</i> threat, especially if one of them is Wolf-Blooded hating Uratha, using Tell to track their spiritual cousins. And humans are shaping Hisil in the most profound way - local politics can reshape your Hunting Grounds in the way you will have real problem to take care on. And let me not <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/432041-werewolf-2e-and-the-internet\">talk about Internet</a>... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> If 1ed were &quot;spirit cops&quot;, then 2ed should be &quot;spirits <b>and humans</b> cops. On THE HUUUUNNTT!&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-10-2015, 06:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T05:15:19-07:00","id":435553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>huntsfromshadow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/434702-question-about-2nd-ed-forsaken#post434702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Similarly what about areas where the Forsaken are not really equipped to be present, say deep in the ocean?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ocean and sea environments are a particular area of the Werewolf world that I would love a chance to cover in detail at some future date.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T05:25:56-07:00","id":435562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/434702-question-about-2nd-ed-forsaken?p=435498#post435498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You must also remember that 2ed is highlighting the humans <b>as a Prey </b>- it's whole shtick of nowdays Iron Masters. Humanity can be <i>bad</i> in setting, on itself. Serial killers are <b>not</b> guided by murder spirits - they are <b>creating</b> murder spirits. Bored and powerful human elite can summon Maeljins and their servants. Humanities hunters are <i>real</i> threat, especially if one of them is Wolf-Blooded hating Uratha, using Tell to track their spiritual cousins. And humans are shaping Hisil in the most profound way - local politics can reshape your Hunting Grounds in the way you will have real problem to take care on. And let me not <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/432041-werewolf-2e-and-the-internet\">talk about Internet</a>... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> If 1ed were &quot;spirit cops&quot;, then 2ed should be &quot;spirits <b>and humans</b> cops. On THE HUUUUNNTT!&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think cop doesn't fit what a werewolf is at all anymore. Werewolf packs and activities bear much more ressemblence to a gang or mafia familiy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T06:08:56-07:00","id":435575,"title":"","content":"If I'm remembering right, the idea is that there are approximately the same number of non-spirit urged serial killers in the WoD as there are on earth. There are also an extra bunch of urged killers <i>on top of</i> this number.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T07:29:20-07:00","id":435663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Felipe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/434702-question-about-2nd-ed-forsaken?p=435562#post435562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think cop doesn't fit what a werewolf is at all anymore. Werewolf packs and activities bear much more ressemblence to a gang or mafia familiy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering the structure, activities, and attitudes of some precincts and groups of police officers can definitely work like a pack, even a malignant one. Watch The Shield or The Wire for examples in fiction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T07:32:26-07:00","id":435667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/434702-question-about-2nd-ed-forsaken?p=434894#post434894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a tree falls in a forest and no one is around to hear it, does it make a sound? Sorry, but I had to. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Without people around to muck around with the world, I think spirits would reflect a world that takes care of itself. I guess their human side keeps them from doing the logical thing, kill all humans. I think the new edition is supposed to move away from &quot;spirit cop.&quot; It sounds more like &quot;spirit predator.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I know I have said this before, but I will do so again. I always saw Werewolf 1st Edition as Spirit PREDATOR and not COP. We never incarcerated spirits, we hunted them and harried them and occasionally killed them. We did not put them in Cuffs and send them to Jail. The image is pretty laughable, really. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T07:36:26-07:00","id":435671,"title":"","content":"Spirit Jail is being bound to a fetish and forced to make yourself useful to society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T07:36:32-07:00","id":435672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/434702-question-about-2nd-ed-forsaken?p=435156#post435156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kind of an interesting question. First edition was ostensibly more about dark mystery than dark brutality. It wasn't like oWoD, where it's our world, but worse, with sin run rampant. It was more our world, but more mysterious. There were conspiracies and things in the shadows, and stranger things behind those things, and even they had strings being pulled by mysterious forces.<br /> <br /> Second edition seems to have kept the mystery but gone and embraced the more evil aspects. The Strix are bad enough when they prey on vampires, but what they do to humanity is often worse. The cults of the God Machine often involve weird sacrifice, maybe even that of life. Of course, it's all happenin through the lens of dark mystery. Or else we wouldn't have so many glorious 'What is this thing?' threads.<br /> <br /> Whether other parts of the world have gone to hell or not is going to depend entirely on your game, but it certainly seems like if there's not werewolves around, the claimed, shartha, ridden or Pure or Bale Hounds or idigam are. Did you read the fiction? Thousands died. It's pretty brutal even when the werewolves are on the hunt. While the writers probably wouldn't do it, it's easy to imagine a lot of the bad aspects of our world magnified by the spirits and other Things of the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> As for the ocean, I don't think nature on its own is a perfect balance. Stuff happens, even without humanity. But there's a lot less stuff probably happening down there, or if it is happening, werewolves wouldn't really be able to see the results until the stars are right or nuclear testing awakens some ancient beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>But isn't that a matter of presentation at table? Your descriptions of 2nd Edition presentation are pretty much what we have in 1st Edition now. It is a style thing, to be sure, and maybe we are just a bit weird at our table (would not be the first time I have heard that). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T08:02:19-07:00","id":435706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/434702-question-about-2nd-ed-forsaken?p=435672#post435672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But isn't that a matter of presentation at table? Your descriptions of 2nd Edition presentation are pretty much what we have in 1st Edition now. It is a style thing, to be sure, and maybe we are just a bit weird at our table (would not be the first time I have heard that). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Just based around what I've heard and done myself, it does seem a lot of people have latched onto the idea that World of Darkness is our world, but worse and more evil. I do it myself as a holdover from reading about old World of Darkness. And as I understand it's a concern in games like Promethean. Why try to be human when being a human means you're going to get murdered or enslaved? But that's effectively homebrew. Aside from a few hiccups, like the Requiem first edition book, first edition seems like it's all more in line with a mysterious world, not necessarily an evil one.<br /> <br /> Until second edition, at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T09:02:21-07:00","id":435766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/434702-question-about-2nd-ed-forsaken?p=435671#post435671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirit Jail is being bound to a fetish and forced to make yourself useful to society.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is one way to explain Fetishes, Yes... Another is a cooperative style wherein the Spirit is made useful to the Uratha for a set period of time. Both work. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T09:05:27-07:00","id":435772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/434702-question-about-2nd-ed-forsaken?p=435706#post435706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just based around what I've heard and done myself, it does seem a lot of people have latched onto the idea that World of Darkness is our world, but worse and more evil. I do it myself as a holdover from reading about old World of Darkness. And as I understand it's a concern in games like Promethean. Why try to be human when being a human means you're going to get murdered or enslaved? But that's effectively homebrew. Aside from a few hiccups, like the Requiem first edition book, first edition seems like it's all more in line with a mysterious world, not necessarily an evil one.<br /> <br /> Until second edition, at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have always viewed nWOD as a Darker Reflection of the World we live in... Yes, it is more mysterious, but it is also darker, more unfriendly, and yes, occasionally more evil. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\